#: includes/admin-page.php:107
msgid "Removes the emoji detection script and styles from the front end, embeds and admin, and stops emoji from being turned into images in feeds and e-mails. Emoji still show as the visitor's own characters."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:108
msgid "Links from one of your posts to another no longer send a pingback to your own site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:109
msgid "Front end only: the ver= value on script and style URLs reveals plugin and WordPress versions. A hash hides them and keeps cache busting after updates. Warning: with Remove, visitors may keep stale CSS and JavaScript from their browser cache after updates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:110
msgid "Your posts can no longer be embedded on other sites, and links to other WordPress sites are no longer turned into embedded frames; providers such as YouTube keep working. Warning: existing embeds of other WordPress sites show as a plain quote with a link."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:111
msgid "Removes the comment reply script from the front end. Warning: the reply link then reloads the page instead of moving the comment form below the comment."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:112
msgid "Removes the Dashicons icon font for logged-out visitors; logged-in users keep it for the toolbar. Warning: themes or plugins that use Dashicons on the front end lose their icons."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:113
msgid "Removes the core block styles on classic themes. Warning: blocks in posts and pages lose their styling unless the theme styles them itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:114
msgid "Removes the global styles CSS (colour, font size and spacing presets) and the block supports CSS on classic themes. Warning: colours, font sizes and spacing chosen in the block editor no longer show, and block layouts such as columns, rows and groups lose their arrangement."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:115
msgid "Heartbeat is the regular check-in of an open admin screen with the server. Optimized keeps every Heartbeat feature at the longest safe interval. Warning: Disabled stops post locking, the login dialog when the session expires, classic editor autosave and nonce refreshes on screens left open for long."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:116
msgid "How many revisions WordPress keeps per post; Site Editor templates, template parts, global styles and navigation keep their full history. Warning: with a limit, older revisions are deleted the next time a post is saved with changes; 0 stops new revisions but keeps existing ones."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:117
msgid "How often the editor autosaves a post; WordPress autosaves every 60 seconds. A longer interval means more unsaved work can be lost if the browser crashes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:118
msgid "Removes the ?p=123 shortlink from the page head and the Link HTTP header."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:119
msgid "Removes the Really Simple Discovery link to xmlrpc.php, which only old blogging clients use."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:120
msgid "Removes the REST API discovery links from the page head and the Link HTTP header; the REST API itself keeps working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:121
msgid "Removes the feed links from the page head; the feeds themselves stay available. Warning: feed readers can no longer find your feeds from the site address alone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:122
msgid "Removes the WordPress version from the generator tag in the page head, feeds and exports."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:123
msgid "Logged-out visitors requesting ?author=N get a 404 instead of a redirect that reveals the author's user name. Only with pretty permalinks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:124
msgid "The REST API user list answers unauthenticated requests with 401, so user names cannot be listed anonymously."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:125
msgid "Embeds of your posts show the site name and address instead of the author's name and profile address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:126
msgid "Removes the user sitemap from the WordPress sitemaps."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:127
msgid "Stops the dashboard from sending your browser's user agent and the site address to WordPress.org to check whether the browser is outdated. The PHP version check stays."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:128
msgid "Removes the WordPress Events and News dashboard widget, which sends an anonymised IP address, locale and timezone to WordPress.org."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:129
msgid "Shows a neutral avatar from this plugin instead of loading Gravatar, so no e-mail hash goes to a third party. Warning: pictures your users and commenters set up on Gravatar no longer show."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:130
msgid "Stores new comments with a shortened IP address (IPv4 /24, IPv6 /48) and without the browser user agent; spam plugins still see the full address. Warning: this cannot be undone for comments stored while it is on, and the comment flood check then works per network, so guests sharing one may be slowed down together."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:131
msgid "YouTube embeds use youtube-nocookie.com and Vimeo embeds get dnt=1. This is not a consent solution."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:132
msgid "The block editor no longer loads the block directory, remote core patterns, the Openverse media category or the Google Fonts collection. Warning: patterns your theme takes from the WordPress.org pattern directory disappear."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:133
msgid "Turns off the AI client built into WordPress, and with it every feature that relies on it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:134
msgid "Unknown user name, unknown e-mail address and wrong password all show the same message, so the login form does not reveal which accounts exist. Messages from other plugins stay."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:135
msgid "Removes the X-Powered-By header (PHP version) on the front end and the X-Redirect-By header from redirects."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:136
msgid "Stops browsers from treating a file as a different type than the server declares."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:137
msgid "Other sites only see your domain, not the full page address, when visitors follow a link. This is what current browsers do anyway."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:138
msgid "Other sites can no longer show your pages in a frame, which protects against clickjacking; WordPress embeds keep working. Warning: tools on other domains that show your site in a frame stop working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:139
msgid "Your pages and the frames in them can no longer ask for camera, microphone or location access. Warning: embedded maps, video calls or forms that need one of these stop working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:140
msgid "Tells browsers to reach this domain only over HTTPS for one year; sent only on HTTPS requests. Warning: a browser that has seen it refuses plain HTTP for a year, even after you switch it off — only use it when HTTPS works for good on this domain."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:141
msgid "Turns off the _jsonp parameter of the REST API, an old cross-domain technique."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:142
msgid "Removes the theme and plugin file editors, so a taken-over admin account cannot change PHP code there. Warning: theme and plugin files then have to be edited another way, for example over SFTP."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:143
msgid "Application passwords let external tools sign in through the REST API. Warning: MCP and Abilities API clients, the WordPress mobile app and integrations that use them stop working for users who lose access."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:144
msgid "Only used when application passwords are limited to selected roles. With no role selected, nobody can use them, administrators included."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:145
msgid "Answers requests to xmlrpc.php with a 403 error and stops advertising the endpoint; trackbacks are refused too. On by default and in every preset, so applying a preset switches it back on; to keep it off for good, set JPKCOM_HARDEN_TRIM_XMLRPC to false in wp-config.php. Warning: Jetpack, the WordPress mobile apps and incoming pingbacks stop working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:146
msgid "Closes comments, pings and trackbacks on every post type and hides existing comments (they are not deleted). The Comments screen, menu, comment counts and comment feeds disappear, and the REST comment routes answer 404. Block editor Notes keep working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:147
msgid "Logged-in users with one of these roles get the unchanged site for the features listed below. By default no role is exempt."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:171
msgid "XML-RPC is already disabled by the JPKCom Disable XML-RPC plugin, so this switch is not needed while that plugin is active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:175
msgid "Comments are already disabled by the JPKCom Disable Comments plugin, so this switch is not needed while that plugin is active."
msgstr ""

